config CP_PMU_PROBE
	tristate "Samsung CP (modem) PMU-only bring-up probe"
	depends on (ARCH_EXYNOS && OF) || COMPILE_TEST
	help
	  Isolated PMU_ALIVE bring-up probe for the CP (Shannon SS310AP
	  modem) domain -- no mailbox, no firmware, no SMC, no SIPC. Exists
	  to answer one question: is CENTRAL_SEQ_CP_STATUS (PMU_ALIVE
	  0x0284) unreachable because nothing has ever issued the CP
	  domain's cal_cp_init() equivalent, or for some other reason? See
	  gnss.md in the tree root, "Downstream sources for CP init and
	  firmware load".

	  This is not a modem driver and never will be -- it does not touch
	  the CP mailbox's IPC channel, does not load firmware, and cannot
	  bring up the cellular stack. Say M here only if you are
	  live-probing this specific PMU question; the offsets it touches
	  have not been individually confirmed safe to read (see the
	  driver's own comments and gnss.md's warnings about hanging the
	  device from untested PMU_ALIVE offsets).
